  "raw_text": "104\n\nKing lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nkingdom\n \n/ reino\n\n(Construct:\n \nKingki lâka\n;\n \nKingkam lâka\n;\n \nKingka lâka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nlfb55\n):\n \nAsiria kingka lâka ba Israel kiamka 10 kingka lâka ba dakbi brin kan\n \n–\n \nThe Assyrian kingdom has captured\nthe Israelite 10 tribe kingdom\n \n/ El reino asirio ha capturado el reino de las 10 tribus israelitas)\n\nGâd Kingka lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nGod’s Kingdom\n \n/ El reino de dios\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nGâd Kingka lâka ba dia daukbia?\n \n–\n \nWhat will God's kingdom do?\n \n/ ¿Qué hará el reino de Dios?)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ntkl\n):\n \nGâd Kingka lâka sturka yamni smalkanka ba tnata yua nani sainka markka tânka tara bri ba kum sa\n \n–\n\nThe preaching of the good news is an important feature of the sign of the last days\n \n/ La predicación de las buenas\n\nnoticias del Reino de Dios es una característica importante de la señal de los\n \nú\nltimos d\ní\nas\n)\n\nKing lâka kyamka wâl\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \n2-tribe kingdom\n \n/ reino de 2 tribus\n\nKing lâka lawana\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nKingdom song\n \n/ canción del reino\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/18\n):\n \nKing Lâka lawanka nani tilara ani ba kau laik sma?\n \n–\n \nWhich of the Kingdom songs do you like\nthe most?\n \n/ ¿Cuál de las canciones de Kingdom te gusta más?)\n\nKing Lâka Sturka Smalki nani Skulka\n \n–\n \nSchool for Kingdom Evangelizers\n \n/ Escuela para Evangelizadores\ndel Reino\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-12/20\n):\n \nPat luki kaikram ki King Lâka Sturka Smalki nani Skulka ra waia dukiara wauhkataya ba\nbanhki dingkaia?\n \n–\n \nHave you already considered filling out and submitting the form for School for Kingdom\nEvangelizers?\n \n/ Ha considerado ya completar y enviar el formulario de Escuela para Evangelizadores del Reino?)\n\nMisaya Kingka lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nMessianic Kingdom\n \n/ Reino mesiánico\n\nKing Lâka sturka yamni ba smalkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto preach/teach the good news of the kingdom\n \n/ predicar/\nenseñar las buenas nuevas del reino\n\nKing lupia mairin\n \n(\nmwb-02/20\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nprincess\n \n/ princesa\n\nKing Nani\n \n(\ndb,dba,bw,dbta\n)\n \n–\n \nKings\n \n(Bible books) / Reyes (libros bíblicos)\n\nKingbaia\n \n(\ndictu\n;\n \nKihngbaia\n-dict\n;\n \nKinhbaia\n-\ndictu-alt\n) (v-trans; intrans:\n \nKingwaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto knock, to knock on a door, to hit, to\nmake a knocking sound, to make a sound by hitting\n \n/ golpear, llamar a la puerta, hacer un sonido de golpe, hacer un\nsonido golpeando\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Matiu 7:7\n):\n \ndur ra kings, bara man nani ra kwâkan kabia\n \n–\n \nknock on the door, and it will be opened to you\n \n/ llamen a la\npuerta, y se les abrirá)\n\nKingwaia\n \n(\ndictu\n;\n \nKihngwaia\n-dict\n;\n \nKinhwaia\n-\ndictu-alt\n) (a/t:\n \nKihngwaia\n) (v-intrans; trans:\n \nKingbaia\n)\n \n–\n \nto be knocked, to be\nhit, to be making a knocking noise, to be making a hitting noise\n \n/ ser golpeado, estar haciendo un ruido de golpe\n\nKipla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nrock, boulder, rapids, torrent\n \n/ roca, rápidos, torrente\n\nKir\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nall around, around\n \n/ todo al rededor, alrededor\n\nKir briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have all around\n \n/ tener todo alrededor\n\nKutbi kir briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have encircling all around\n \n/ tener rodeando todo alrededor\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Hibru Nani 12:1\n):\n \nWitnis ailal kutbi kir wan brisa\n \n–\n \nWe have many witnesses encircling all around us\n \n/\nTenemos muchos testigos rodeándonos a nuestro alrededor)\n\nKir kutbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto completely surround, to encircle all around\n \n/ rodear completamente, rodear todo\n\nTnaya kir\n \n(a/t:\n \nNaya kir\n,\n \nSnaya kir\n) (adv)\n \n–\n \nall around, all around the side\n \n/ todo al redodor, todo en derredor\n\nAi tnaya kir\n \n–\n \nall around him/her/it\n \n/ a su alrededor\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlff-29\n):\n \nUpla kum aiska pali yapuya taim, ai tnaya kir ra dîa taki ba nu âpu sa.\n \n–\n \nWhen a person is really\nsleeping (deeply), they are not aware of what is happening around them.\n \n/ Cuando una persona está bien\ndormida (durmiendo profundamente), no se da cuenta de lo que sucede a su alrededor.)\n\nWan tnaya kir\n \n–\n \nall around us\n \n/ a nuestro alrededor\n\nKira\n \n(fs/ea:\n \nKirra\n)\n \n–\n \na suffix that adds the idea of\n \nabounding in\n \nthe quality referred to / un sufijo que agrega la idea de\n\nabundar en\n \nla calidad referida\n\nKira\n \n(adv)\n \n–\n \nwith, together with, abounding in\n \n/ con, junto con, abundando en\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb32\n):\n \nJael tawa pali lamara wan, bin daukras kira, ...\n \n–\n \nJael went close very slowly, without making a sound, ...\n \n/ Jael se\nacercó muy lentamente, sin hacer ruido, ...)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-07/20\n):\n \nFero ba tara pulan lâka brin sakuna ai dara walras kira Gâd kupia lâka aimakbia hilp munan\n \n–\n \nPharaoh had\n\narrogance but unconsciously, he helped fulfill God’s will\n \n/ Faraón tenía arrogancia pero inconscientemente, ayudó a que se\ncumpliera la voluntad de Dios)\n\nÂpu kira\n \n(Apu kira, Apukira)\n \n(a/t:\n \nÂpukira\n)\n \n–\n \nwithout having, not having, having nothing\n \n/ sin tener, no tener, no tener\nnada",
